# HEM-7530T (Z identity): reconnect with a saved key; setting-information block 3 fails its checksum.
# OpenPressure does not trust the index and falls back to a full sweep of the bank; Omron Connect rejects the
# index (expect omron rejected).
# Omron selects HEM-7530T-Z from the advertised IDs (category 0x0000, model 0x0151);
# OpenPressure maps the Device Information model HEM-7530T-Z to its HEM-7530T map (14-byte records).
name hem-7530t/connect-bad-index-checksum
flow connect
advertise name=BLEsmart_000001510011223344 services=ecbe3980-c9a2-11e1-b1bd-0002a5d5c51b
# Synthetic Device Information; Omron reads the revisions and the System ID during connection setup.
dis model=HEM-7530T-Z firmware=0001 software=0001 systemid=0011223344556677
time 2026-01-02T03:04:05 zone=UTC
key 05050505050505050505050505050505

alias unlock b305b680-aee7-11e1-a730-0002a5d5c51b
alias tx db5b55e0-aee7-11e1-965e-0002a5d5c51b,e0b8a060-aee7-11e1-92f4-0002a5d5c51b,0ae12b00-aee8-11e1-a192-0002a5d5c51b,10e1ba60-aee8-11e1-89e5-0002a5d5c51b
alias rx 49123040-aee8-11e1-a74d-0002a5d5c51b,4d0bf320-aee8-11e1-a0d9-0002a5d5c51b,5128ce60-aee8-11e1-b84b-0002a5d5c51b,560f1420-aee8-11e1-8184-0002a5d5c51b
alias clock 00002a2b-0000-1000-8000-00805f9b34fb

# 14-byte records with adjacent byte pairs swapped (Omron reverseSendData=1; OpenPressure reads big-endian):
# 130/78 mmHg, pulse 67, 2025-07-09 06:14:38, sequence number 1, Omron record checksum 00 at offset 12.
memory fill=ff
memory 0x2e8 4e691943 1d2603a6 0000 0001 0000
# Index block (index_setting_read_address=260), byte pairs swapped like the records: next write position 1,
# one unsent record, sequence number 1.
memory 0x260 0001 0000 0001 0000 00010000
# Setting-info block 3 is checksummed like a record (8-bit sum of bytes 0-13 in byte 14); blocks 1 and 2 are
# exempt (OtherInfo ignoreCheckSumBlocks). Here the logical block sums to 05 but its checksum byte (logical 14,
# wire 0x29b) is 00; the 05 sits in the other byte of that swapped pair (logical 15, wire 0x29a). Summing the
# wire bytes 0-13 into wire byte 14 would accept this block, summing the logical bytes rejects it.
memory 0x28c 05000000000000000000000000000500

[omron-only: Omron 2026.09.03 sends 02 (confirm encryption) before authenticating, observed in the sandbox] write unlock 02 00000000000000000000000000000000
[omron-only: acknowledgment for the confirm-encryption frame above] notify unlock 8200
write unlock 01 05050505050505050505050505050505
notify unlock 8100

write tx 08 00 00 00 00 10 00 18
notify rx 18 80 00 00 00 10 00 01 02 03 04 05 06 07 08 09 0a 0b 0c 0d 0e 0f 00 88

[omron-only: Omron reads the index block (index_setting_read_address 0x260) before records] reads 0x260 44 chunk=44
[omron-only: Omron reads setting-info blocks 3 and 4 (index_setting_info_read_address 0x270 + 28, 16 + 8 bytes)] reads 0x28c 24 chunk=24

[ours-only: index-driven read: OpenPressure reads the 68-byte settings/index image at 0x260 in 56-byte blocks; Omron reads 44 bytes plus blocks 3 and 4] reads 0x260 68 chunk=56
[ours-only: the block-3 checksum fails, so OpenPressure does not trust the index and sweeps every slot of the bank in 56-byte blocks] reads 0x2e8 1260 chunk=56

[ours-only: OpenPressure clock sync via Current Time; Omron writes setting block 3 instead (docs/omron-sandbox.md)] write clock ea 07 01 02 03 04 05 05 00 01

# Omron Connect 2026.09.03 reports "CheckSumError OGSCMemoryMapAnalyzer.checkSettingReadIndex" after reading block 3,
# sends its error END and disconnects without reading records. OpenPressure ends the session normally after the sweep.
[omron-only: Omron 2026.09.03 error END after rejecting the block-3 checksum (CheckSumError checkSettingReadIndex), observed in the sandbox] write tx 08 0f ff ff ff 00 00 f8
[omron-only: synthetic acknowledgment of the error END; the physical monitor reply is unconfirmed] notify rx 08 8f ff ff ff 00 00 78
[ours-only: OpenPressure falls back to a full sweep and ends normally; Omron rejects the index and sends its error END] write tx 08 0f 00 00 00 00 00 07
[ours-only: acknowledgment for the normal END above] notify rx 08 8f 00 00 00 00 00 87

expect omron rejected
[ours-only: Omron rejects the index (block-3 checksum) before reading records; OpenPressure decodes the record from its fallback sweep] expect reading user=1 sys=130 dia=78 pulse=67 time=2025-07-09T06:14:38
